A||N||6||Butter||V8 Fiero Gets beat by a Tricycle!||||11||
Z||000000||Butter||11-02-2001||12:37 PM||||Thought yall might enjoy a recap of a run I did yesterday.  Also something not to tangle with.<P>Anyways,<BR>Yesterday after work as I was getting on the four lane and I noticed this Really nice Yellow Tricycle peddling down the four lane.  I wanted to see it a little closer so I ease around it in the left lane with a thumb up, Nice show quality Trike.  Just so happens we are going the same way for a while and I noticed after I passed he looked over as if his curiousity peeked and stays kinda close eventually passing me back.  As traffic would have it we happen to line up at a stop sign with no other traffic around and he looks over and grins threw a gray beard.  I smile back and we ease threw the intersection and I begin to accelerate as much as possible without breaking traction till the pedal hits the floor.  I notice he just wont let me get in front as I can see the throttle linkage going to the V8 powered trike being feathered.  We run em' up to about 70 back out and waive at one another as we were going our different ways.<P>It was fun but I knew better than to mess much with a Boss Hog.  Friend of mine has a nice one and yes they are Quick.  Lesson for the day, a V8 with 3 wheels is faster than a V8 with 4 wheels.||||reg||11
Z||000001||avengador1||11-02-2001||02:19 PM||||Not to be a smartass,no flame intended by me, but isn't the Boss hoss a two wheel motorcycle with a 350 V-8?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Butter||11-02-2001||03:24 PM||||avengador1,<BR>You are more or less correct.  But after seeing some of those Hogs it just looks like one topped out and is ready to go to the sale barn I mean Sail Hard.  Maybe somebody put one on steroids, Huh!<BR> <BR>They sure fast anyway! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <BR>||||reg||12
Z||000003||Philphine||11-02-2001||06:40 PM||||they make trikes too. saw one at a car show. had a '63 vette rear body style.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Ronnie||11-03-2001||12:00 AM||||Just to let everyone know, they make Boss Hoss motorcycles and trikes with the 502 BBlock now with over 600 hp!! Not to be messed with. Don't know how they handle that much hp , but wouldn't want to throw my leg across that much hp.Next time you see one, better take a closer look at the engine.Of course, a 350 on that light of a vehicle would be enough to dust any Fiero I think.||||reg||6
Z||000005||avengador1||11-03-2001||11:13 AM||||I saw one at Englishtown N.J. once and it practically stood up by itself because of the wide rear tire it had. I definitly would not want to race against it as it basically is a motor with wheels.||||reg||1
Z||000006||stimpy||11-03-2001||01:39 PM||||I'd think the HP would even out against the weight of the solid brass balls the rider would have to have to ride one of those. VERY SCARY!||||reg||6
